  "details": "# How to reproduce:\n\n1. Create a render texture with BindMS set to true and AntiAliasing set to None (BindMS can be modified using the debug inspector).\n\n2. Attach a camera to the avatar and set the previously created render texture as its render target.\n\n3. Attach a quad for visualizing the rendered texture.\n\nYou can find a Unitypackage containing the necessary materials in the following link:\n\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1QXjf2gHTtemvqlRKwWMlvQhdof5ZD21F/view?usp=drive_link\n\n# Expected behavior\n\n- The quad should display the image captured by the camera.\n\n- This worked as expected in Unity 2019.\n\n# Actual behavior\n\n- The quad appears to be filled with a black image.\n\n# Environment\n\n- VRChat Build 1373\n\n- VRCSDK 3.4.1",
